{
  "id": "fork-pr-missing-secret",
  "title": "Coverage upload fails on a fork PR: COVERAGE_TOKEN secret is not passed to fork workflows",
  "description": "A contributor's pull_request from the fork contributor-fork/sdk-python adds retry jitter. Lint and the whole test matrix pass (19 passed in the failing job too); only the 3.12 job's 'Upload coverage' step fails with '##[error]Input required and not supplied: token'. The step passes token: ${{ secrets.COVERAGE_TOKEN }}, and GitHub does not expose repository secrets to pull_request workflows triggered from forks, so the input is empty (the log's 'Secret source: None' and the empty 'token:' input echo show it). Main-branch history is green and the diff does not touch CI. Fix belongs in .github/workflows/ci.yml: skip the upload (or make it non-fatal / tokenless) when the PR comes from a fork, e.g. if: github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.repository. Not a code problem and not flaky.",
